@@ -9336,3 +9336,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE D (CROSS-DOMAIN DETECTION CALIBRATION; complementary; cached; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- REPAIR the .406 false calibrated-multi-domain detector contract with PROPER pools + base-rate separation (Semantic Confidence Aggregation arXiv:2602.07842). .406 (exp4397) reported detection_calibrated_multi_domain=false, but the failure was CONFOUNDED: code_humaneval detection AUROC was 0.98 yet underpowered (n=100) and the multi-valid-output / base-rate effects were not separated from genuine calibration failure. This attempt: (1) build PROPER pools from EXISTING cached candidates -- code (HumanEval, cached exp1999/2838/2839, n>=300) + GSM8K (cached, n>=300) -- NOT the underpowered n=100; (2) apply SEMANTIC CONFIDENCE AGGREGATION (aggregate the verifier's confidence across semantically-equivalent valid answers / verifier-success modes BEFORE calibration) + per-domain BASE-RATE + answer-cardinality metadata, so calibration failure is separated from multi-valid-output/base-rate effects; (3) leave-one-domain-out calibration (Platt/temperature fit on the other domains) and report detection AUROC + risk-coverage + expected-calibration-error per domain. Emit detection_calibrated_multi_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=2 NON-FoVer domains AND leave-one-domain-out calibration keeps ECE below the uncalibrated baseline on the held-out domain, AFTER base-rate/multi-valid separation). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = a deployable multi-domain detector contract (the verifier-domain-expansion step, north-star §0 step 2); a domain at chance is LOGGED as a missing-verifier gap (the product backlog). This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO new live inference; NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: calibrated_multi_domain_contract_false_deconfounded; results/experiment_4408_cross_domain_detection_calibration_repair.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE E1 (SOTA-ingestion; mandatory per SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline) -- ingest the SOTA for the .407 bleeding-edge forks (REAL-intervention first-error localizer deconfounding; cross-domain detection calibration; active-learning localizer compounding; ARC E3 per-mechanic-unit-test deeper solves) and MAP the strongest 3-5 methods onto the .408 roadmap, conditioned on the .407 outcomes (did the REAL-intervention localizer GENUINELY beat the position-only baseline + generalize cross-domain? did active selection COMPOUND? did the repaired calibration hold multi-domain? did ARC reach deeper/tail levels via per-mechanic unit tests?). Use the RELIABLE channel ONLY (scripts/sweep_clusters.py / sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch) -- /deep-research is BANNED in-loop. Every method MUST carry a real, VERIFIED arXiv ID/URL (no citation = fabrication). FLAG A2D2 (2606.13565) + SEPO (2502.01384) verifier-as-reward GENERATOR-training as OUT-OF-BAND/operator-owned. Update research-studying.md (mark ingested) and emit flagged_for_v408 (the single strongest method for the .408 planner). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: sota_ingestion_v408_mapped; results/experiment_4409_sota_ingestion_v408.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE E2 (INFRA/HYGIENE) -- registry/gaps hygiene + GAP-4 regression guard. (1) Reconcile ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md + ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml with the .407 outcomes (the deconfounded localizer exp4403/4404 -- move GAP-FOVER-BIPRM-LOCALIZATION to status: filled if the localizer GENUINELY localized + generalized, or sharpen it if it retired as position-bound; the active-learning compounding result exp4407; the repaired cross-domain calibration + any new chance-detection gaps exp4408; new ARC reproduced levels + per-mechanic-test gaps from exp4405/4406). (2) Run the GAP-4 execution regression guard (the ARC oracle-distinct verifier-beats-vote result must not silently regress). (3) Verify the capstone verifier_is_oracle stamping fix is STILL durable (the .402 exp4355 fix; confirm the .407 capstone path inherits it). Use the robust aggregate-available helper (read available artifacts, report gaps -- do NOT hard-block all-False if one is missing). Emit regression_guard_passed BARE bool. NO production verifier edits (audit-only per Verifier Authenticity Discipline). (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_registry_unreadable; results/experiment_4410_registry_gaps_hygiene_gap4_guard.json
+- 2026-06-18: PHASE E3 (HARDWARE CONTINUITY; KV260 opportunistic per north-star §3) -- KV260 SSH-reachability + loaded-bitstream continuity check. Per north-star §3, KV260 is THE sovereignty story (drive to terminal, then freeze); GateMate/PolarFire are opportunistic-only. SSH-reachability precondition ONLY (NEVER a host SD-card precondition per KV260 SSH-Not-SD-Card Discipline). If the board is reachable, record the loaded overlay (xmutil listapps) + a lightweight liveness check (the carnot_ising bitstream UIO device present). If unreachable -> honest_verdict blocked_kv260_ssh_unreachable (a clean documented skip, NOT a fabrication). This keeps the board visible in the milestone retro without burning a deep task slot. NO host SD-card-device precondition (the retired mechanism). NO TRM training. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success_kv260_continuity_terminal_reached; results/experiment_4411_hardware_continuity_kv260.json
